<v Russell Banks>That scene, at Osgood's Lounge in Concord, ended with Ron's departure alone after having bought Sarah a second drink and Sarah's return to her friends in the booth. I don't know what she told them, but it's not hard to imagine. The three women were not close friends-- merely fellow workers at Rumford Press, where they stood at the end of a long conveyor belt, day after day, packing TV Guides into cartons.
<v Russell Banks>那个发生在康科德奥斯古德酒廊的场景，以罗恩在给她买了第二杯酒后独自离开，莎拉回到卡座的朋友身边而告终。我不知道她跟她们说了什么，但并不难想象。这三个女人并不是密友——只是Rumford Press的同事，她们在那里站在长长的传送带尽头，日复一日地把《电视指南》装进纸箱。

00:25:34.100 --> 00:25:56.210
<v Russell Banks>They all hated their jobs, and frequently after work, when they worked the day shift, they put on the cowboy hats and boots, which they kept all day in their lockers, and stopped for a drink or two on their way home. This had been their first visit to Osgood's, however, a place that prior to this, they had avoided out of a sneering belief that no one went there but lawyers and insurance men.
<v Russell Banks>她们都讨厌自己的工作，经常在下班后，当她们上白班时，她们会穿上牛仔帽和靴子——她们整天把这些放在储物柜里——然后在回家路上停下来喝一两杯。然而，这是她们第一次来奥斯古德，一个在此之前她们因为一种不屑的偏见而避开的地方，觉得除了律师和保险从业者，没人会去那里。

