00:48:23.560 --> 00:48:25.670
<v Russell Banks>"Hello?"
<v Russell Banks>“喂？”

00:48:25.670 --> 00:48:27.200
<v Russell Banks>"Hi."
<v Russell Banks>“嗨。”

00:48:27.200 --> 00:48:29.360
<v Russell Banks>"How are you doing?"
<v Russell Banks>“你怎么样？”

00:48:29.360 --> 00:48:32.750
<v Russell Banks>"OK, I guess. A little tired.
<v Russell Banks>“还行，我想。有点累。”

00:48:32.750 --> 00:48:34.490
<v Russell Banks>"Still hungover?"
<v Russell Banks>“还有宿醉吗？”

00:48:34.490 --> 00:48:39.940
<v Russell Banks>"No, not really. Just tired. I hate Mondays."
<v Russell Banks>“不，没有。只是累。我讨厌周一。”

00:48:39.940 --> 00:48:42.440
<v Russell Banks>"You have fun last night?"
<v Russell Banks>“昨晚玩得开心吗？”

00:48:42.440 --> 00:48:55.140
<v Russell Banks>"Well yes, sort of. It's nice out there at the lake. Listen," she says, brightening. "Why don't you come over here tonight? The kids are all going out later, but if you come over before eight, you can meet them. They really want to meet you."
<v Russell Banks>“嗯，是的，还行。湖边风景不错。听着，”她亮起声音说。“你今晚为什么不过来？孩子们晚点都要出去，如果你八点前过来，你可以见见他们。他们真的很想见你。”

00:48:55.140 --> 00:48:57.240
<v Russell Banks>"You told them about me?"
<v Russell Banks>“你告诉他们我的事了？”

00:48:57.240 --> 00:49:01.480
<v Russell Banks>"Sure, a long time ago. I'm not supposed to tell my own kids?"
<v Russell Banks>“当然，很久以前了。我不该告诉我的孩子们吗？”

00:49:01.480 --> 00:49:04.110
<v Russell Banks>Ron is silent.
<v Russell Banks>罗恩沉默了。

00:49:04.110 --> 00:49:13.690
<v Russell Banks>She says, "You don't want to come over here tonight. You don't want to meet my kids. No, you don't want my kids to meet you, that's it.
<v Russell Banks>她说：“你今晚不想过来。你不想见我的孩子。不，你不想让我的孩子见你，就是这样。”

00:49:13.690 --> 00:49:18.910
<v Russell Banks>"No, no. It's just, I've got a lot of work to do."
<v Russell Banks>“不，不。只是，我有好多工作要做。”

00:49:18.910 --> 00:49:23.100
<v Russell Banks>"We should talk," she announces in a flat voice.
<v Russell Banks>“我们得谈谈，”她平淡地宣布。

00:49:23.100 --> 00:49:25.910
<v Russell Banks>"Yes," he says. "We should talk."
<v Russell Banks>“是的，”他说。“我们得谈谈。”

00:49:25.910 --> 00:49:34.100
<v Russell Banks>They agree that she will meet him at his apartment and they'll talk, and they say goodbye and hang up.
<v Russell Banks>他们商定她会在他的公寓见他，他们谈谈，于是道别挂了电话。

00:49:34.100 --> 00:50:13.550
<v Russell Banks>While Ron is heating his supper and then eating it alone at his kitchen table, and Sarah is feeding her children, perhaps I should admit, since we are nearing the end of my story, that I don't actually know that Sarah Cole is dead. A few years ago, I happened to run into one of her friends from the Press, a blond woman with an underslung jaw. Her name, she reminded me, was Glenda. She had seen me at Osgood's a couple of times, and we had met at the El Rancho once, when I had gone there with Sarah. We were standing outside the Sears store on South Main Street, where I'd gone to buy paint. I had recently remarried, and my wife and I were redecorating my apartment.
<v Russell Banks>当罗恩在加热晚餐然后一个人在厨房桌子吃时，而莎拉在喂她的孩子，也许我该承认，既然我的故事接近尾声，我其实并不知道莎拉·科尔已经去世了。几年前，我恰好碰到了她在印刷厂的朋友之一，一个下巴下垂的金发女人。她的名字，她提醒我，是格伦达。她在奥斯古德见过我几次，我们在埃尔牧场见过一次，当时我是和莎拉一起去的。我们站在南大街西尔斯商店外面，我去那里买漆。我最近再婚了，我和妻子正在重新装饰我的公寓。

00:50:13.550 --> 00:50:17.770
<v Russell Banks>"Whatever happened to Sarah?" I ask Glenda. "Is she still down at the Press?"
<v Russell Banks>“莎拉后来怎么样了？”我问格伦达。“她还在印刷厂吗？”

00:50:17.770 --> 00:50:28.710
<v Russell Banks>"Jeez, no. She left a long time ago, way back. I heard she went back with her ex-husband. I can't remember his name. Something Cole. Eddie Cole, maybe."
<v Russell Banks>“天哪，没有。她很久以前就离开了，很早以前。我听说她回到她前夫身边了。我不记得他的名字。叫什么科尔。也许叫艾迪·科尔。”

00:50:28.710 --> 00:50:52.040
<v Russell Banks>I asked her if she was sure of that, and she said no. She'd only heard it around the bars and at the Press. But she assumed it was true. People said Sarah had moved back with her ex-husband and was living for a while with him and the kids in a trailer in a park near Hooksett, and then when the kids, or at least the boys, get out of school, the rest of them moved down to Florida or someplace, because he was out of work. He was a carpenter, she thought.
<v Russell Banks>我问她是否确定，她说不。她只是在酒吧和印刷厂听说的。但她认为是真的。人们说莎拉搬回去和前夫一起住，有一阵子和他在胡克塞特附近公园里的拖车里带着孩子住，然后当孩子们，或者至少是男孩们，走出学校后，剩下的人搬去了佛罗里达或者别的地方，因为他失业了。她认为他是个木匠。

00:50:52.040 --> 00:50:54.480
<v Russell Banks>"He was mean to her," I said.
<v Russell Banks>“他对她不好，”我说。

00:50:54.480 --> 00:51:05.620
<v Russell Banks>"Oh, well, yeah. He was a bastard, all right. I met him a couple times and I didn't like him. Short, ugly, and mean when he got drunk. But you know what they say."
<v Russell Banks>“噢，嗯，是的。他是个混蛋，没错。我见过他几次，我不喜欢他。矮、丑，喝醉了就很刻薄。但你知道他们说什么。”

00:51:05.620 --> 00:51:07.870
<v Russell Banks>"What do they say?"
<v Russell Banks>“他们说什么？”

00:51:07.870 --> 00:51:11.580
<v Russell Banks>"Oh, you know. About water seeking its own level and all."
<v Russell Banks>“噢，你知道。关于物以类聚，人以群分什么的。”

00:51:11.580 --> 00:51:15.070
<v Russell Banks>"Sarah wasn't mean, drunk or sober."
<v Russell Banks>“莎拉不刻薄，不管醉酒还是清醒。”

00:51:15.070 --> 00:51:19.120
<v Russell Banks>The woman laughed. "Nah, but she sure was short and ugly."
<v Russell Banks>那个女人笑了。“那倒不，但她确实矮小而且丑陋。”

00:51:19.120 --> 00:51:19.930
<v Russell Banks>I said nothing.
<v Russell Banks>我什么都没说。

00:51:19.930 --> 00:51:35.440
<v Russell Banks>"Hey, don't get me wrong," Glenda said. "I liked Sarah. But you and her-- well, you sure made a funny-looking couple. She probably didn't feel so self-conscious and all with her husband," she said somberly.
<v Russell Banks>“嘿，别误会我的意思，”格伦达说。“我喜欢莎拉。但你和她——好吧，你们看起来确实是一对滑稽的夫妇。她可能在丈夫身边没那么自卑，”她阴郁地说。

00:51:35.440 --> 00:51:40.220
<v Russell Banks>"Well. I loved her," I said.
<v Russell Banks>“好吧。我爱她，”我说。

00:51:40.220 --> 00:52:04.050
<v Russell Banks>The woman raised one plucked eyebrow in disbelief. She smiled. "Sure you did, honey," she said, and she patted me on the arm. "Sure you did." Then she let the smile drift off her face, turned, and walked away from me.
<v Russell Banks>女人怀疑地扬起一只画过的眉毛。她笑了。“你当然爱，亲爱的，”她说，拍了拍我的胳膊。“你当然爱。”然后她任由笑容从脸上淡去，转身走开了。

00:52:04.050 --> 00:52:26.080
<v Russell Banks>When someone you have loved dies, you accept the fact of her death, but then the person goes on living in your memory, dreams, and reveries. You have imaginary conversations with her. You see something striking and remind yourself to tell your loved one about it, and then get brought up short by the fact of her death. And at night, in your sleep, the dead person visits you.
<v Russell Banks>当某位你爱过的人去世时，你接受她死亡的事实，但那个人会继续活在你的记忆、梦境和沉思中。你会和她进行想象中的对话。你看到引人注目的东西，提醒自己要告诉爱人，然后因她死亡的事实而猛然停住。晚上在睡梦中，死去的人会来看你。

00:52:26.080 --> 00:53:14.510
<v Russell Banks>With Sarah, none of that happened. When she was gone from my life, she was gone absolutely, as if she had never existed in the first place. It was only later, when I could think of her as dead, I could come out and say it-- "my friend Sarah Cole is dead"-- that I was able to tell this story. For that is when she began to enter my memories, my dreams and reveries. In that way, I learned that I truly did love her, and now I have begun to grieve over her death, to wish her alive again, so that I can say to her the things I could not know or say when she was alive, when I did not know that I loved her.
<v Russell Banks>对于莎拉，这些都没有发生。当她从我的生活中消失时，她完全消失了，仿佛她从来没有存在过一样。直到后来，当我能想到她已经去世，能够走出来并说出它——“我已故的朋友莎拉·科尔”——我才能够讲述这个故事。因为那时她才开始进入我的记忆、梦境和沉思。通过那种方式，我得知我确实爱她，现在我已经开始为她的死感到悲伤，希望她再活过来，这样我就能对她说出那些在她还活着时我无法知道或说出的事情，那时我不知道我爱她。

00:53:14.510 --> 00:53:36.810
<v Russell Banks>The woman arrives at Ron's apartment around eight. There was a soft knock at his door. He opens it, turns away, and crosses to the kitchen, where he turns back, lights a cigarette, and watches her. She closes the door. He offers her a drink, which she declines, and somewhat formally, he invites her to sit down.
<v Russell Banks>那个女人在大约八点到达罗恩的公寓。门上轻轻敲了几下。他打开门，转身，走到厨房，转过身，点了一根烟，看着她。她关上门。他递给她一杯酒，她拒绝了，并相当正式地，他邀请她坐下。

00:53:36.810 --> 00:53:53.570
<v Russell Banks>She sits carefully on the sofa, in the middle with her feet close together on the floor, as if being interviewed for a job. He comes around and sits in the easy chair, relaxed, one leg slung over the other at the knee, as if he were interviewing her for the job.
<v Russell Banks>她小心地坐在沙发中间，脚在地上靠在一起，仿佛正在参加工作面试。他走过来坐在休闲椅里，放松，一只脚在膝盖处搭在另一只脚上，仿佛他正在面试她。

00:53:53.570 --> 00:53:57.240
<v Russell Banks>"Well," he says. "you wanted to talk."
<v Russell Banks>“好吧，”他说。“你想谈谈。”

00:53:57.240 --> 00:54:04.750
<v Russell Banks>"Yes. But now you're mad at me. I can see that. I didn't do anything wrong."
<v Russell Banks>“是的。但你现在对我生气了。我看得出来。我没做错什么。”

00:54:04.750 --> 00:54:07.240
<v Russell Banks>"I'm not mad at you."
<v Russell Banks>“我没有对你生气。”

00:54:07.240 --> 00:54:16.780
<v Russell Banks>They are silent for a moment. Ron goes on smoking his cigarette. Finally she sighs and says, "You don't want to see me anymore, do you."
<v Russell Banks>他们沉默了一会儿。罗恩继续抽烟。终于她叹了口气说：“你不想再见我了，是吗。”

00:54:16.780 --> 00:54:33.960
<v Russell Banks>He waits a few seconds and answers. "Yes. That's right." Getting up from the chair, he walks to the silver gray bicycle and stands before it, running a fingertip along the slender crossbar from the saddle to the chrome-plated handlebars.
<v Russell Banks>他等了几秒钟回答。“是的。就是这样。”从椅子上站起，他走向银灰色的自行车，站在它前面，从车座到镀铬的车把，用指尖沿着纤细的横杆划过。

00:54:33.960 --> 00:55:16.250
<v Russell Banks>"You're a son of a bitch," she says in a low voice. "You're worse than my ex-husband." Then she smiles meanly, almost sneers, and soon he realizes that she is telling him that she won't leave. He's stuck with her, she informs him with cold precision. "You think I'm just so much meat, and all you've got to do is call up the butcher shop and cancel your order. Well, now you're going to find out different. You can't cancel your order. I'm not meat. I'm not one of your pretty little girlfriends who come running when you want them and go away when you get tired of them. I'm different. I got nothing to lose, Ron. Nothing. So you're stuck with me, Ron."
<v Russell Banks>“你是个混蛋，”她低声说。“你比我前夫还糟。”然后她刻薄地笑了，几乎在嘲笑，很快他意识到她是在告诉他她不会离开。她带着冰冷的精确感告诉他，他被她缠住了。“你以为我只是一块肉，你所要做的就是给肉店打电话取消订单。好吧，现在你会发现不同的。你取消不了订单。我不是肉。我不是你那些想要时就跑过来，当你厌倦时就走开的漂亮小女朋友。我是不同的。我一无所有，罗恩。什么都没有。所以你被我缠住了，罗恩。”

00:55:16.250 --> 00:55:24.270
<v Russell Banks>She sits back in the couch and crosses her legs at the ankles. "I think I will have that drink you offered."
<v Russell Banks>她坐在沙发里，脚踝处交叉双腿。“我想我要喝你提供的那杯酒。”

00:55:24.270 --> 00:55:28.870
<v Russell Banks>"Look, Sarah. It would be better if you go now."
<v Russell Banks>“听着，莎拉。你现在走比较好。”

00:55:28.870 --> 00:55:40.820
<v Russell Banks>"No," she says flatly. "You offered me a drink when I came in. Nothing's changed since I've been here, not for me and not for you. I'd like that drink you offered," she says haughtily.
<v Russell Banks>“不，”她平淡地说。“你刚进来时提供了酒。我在这里时什么都没变，对我来说没变，对你也一样。我想要你提供的那杯酒，”她傲慢地说。

00:55:40.820 --> 00:55:52.820
<v Russell Banks>Ron turns away from the bicycle and takes a step toward her. His face has stiffened into a mask. "Enough is enough," he says through clenched teeth. "I've given you enough."
<v Russell Banks>罗恩转过身离开自行车，向她走了一步。他的脸僵硬成了一个面具。“适可而止，”他咬着牙说。“我已经给了你够多了。”

00:55:52.820 --> 00:55:57.020
<v Russell Banks>"Fix me a drink, will you, honey?" she says with a phony smile.
<v Russell Banks>“帮我倒杯酒，好吗，亲爱的？”她假笑着说。

00:55:57.020 --> 00:56:33.860
<v Russell Banks>Ron orders her to leave. She refuses. He grabs her by the arm and yanks her to her feet. She starts crying lightly. She stands there and looks up into his face and weeps. But she does not move toward the door, so he pushes her. She regains her balance and goes on weeping. He stands back, and places his fists on his hips, and looks at her. "Go on. Go on and leave, you ugly bitch," he says to her. He says the words again, almost tenderly. "Leave, you ugly bitch."
<v Russell Banks>罗恩命令她离开。她拒绝了。他抓住她的胳膊把她拉起来。她开始轻声哭泣。她站在那儿抬头看着他的脸哭泣。但她没有走向门口，于是他推了她一下。她恢复了平衡继续哭泣。他退后一步，把拳头放在臀部，看着她。“走吧。走吧，离开这儿，你这丑陋的婊子，”他对她说。他又重复了那些话，几乎是温柔地。“离开，你这丑陋的婊子。”

00:56:33.860 --> 00:56:52.670
<v Russell Banks>Her hair is golden, her brown eyes deep and sad, her mouth full and affectionate, her tears the tears of love and loss, and her pleading, outstretched arms, her entire body, the arms and body of a devoted woman's cruelly rejected love.
<v Russell Banks>她的头发是金色的，棕色的眼睛深邃而悲伤，嘴巴丰满而充满感情，她的眼泪是爱与失落的眼泪，她那恳求的、伸出的双臂，她整个身体，都是一个深情女人被残忍拒绝的爱的双臂和身体。

00:56:52.670 --> 00:57:00.420
<v Russell Banks>A third time he says the words. "Leave me now, you disgusting, ugly bitch."
<v Russell Banks>他第三次说了那些话。“现在离开我，你这令人作呕的、丑陋的婊子。”

00:57:00.420 --> 00:57:18.290
<v Russell Banks>She is wrapped in an envelope of golden light, a warm, dense haze that she seems to have stepped into as into a carriage. And then she is gone and he is alone again.
<v Russell Banks>她被包裹在金色的光芒中，一层温暖、浓重的迷雾，她似乎像进入马车一样走进了它。然后她消失了，他又回到了孤独之中。

00:57:18.290 --> 00:57:43.010
<v Russell Banks>He looks around the room, searching for her. Sitting down in the easy chair, he places his face in his hands. It's not as if she has died. It's as if he has killed her.
<v Russell Banks>他环顾房间，寻找她。坐在休闲椅里，他双手捂脸。这不是她死了。而是仿佛他杀了她。

00:57:43.010 --> 00:57:51.480
<v Ira Glass>Russell Banks, reading from his short story "Sarah Cole: A Type of Love Story." The full, unedited version of this story is in his collection The Angel on the Roof.
<v Ira Glass>拉塞尔·班克斯，朗读他的短篇小说《莎拉·科尔：一种爱情故事》。这个故事的完整、未删节版本在他的文集《屋顶上的天使》中。

